<p><strong>ChatGPT Ads, Google Ads and Meta Ads reach people in different environments.</strong> ChatGPT can reach a person during a conversation, Google can capture active search demand, and Meta can create discovery in social feeds. The best platform depends on the customer's mindset and the campaign's job.</p>
<p>Start with the <a href="/blog/chatgpt-ads-india">complete ChatGPT Ads India guide</a> if the new channel is unfamiliar, or read the <a href="/blog/chatgpt-ads-cost-india">India pricing and budget guide</a> before comparing campaign economics.</p>

<h2>The biggest difference is user behaviour</h2>
<h3>ChatGPT Ads: conversation and consideration</h3>
<p>A user may be explaining a problem, learning, comparing options or narrowing a decision. OpenAI says ad delivery can use the context and intent of the current conversation along with creative and landing-page signals. Context hints help describe relevant conversation themes but are not exact-match keywords.</p>
<h3>Google Ads: active search demand</h3>
<p>A user expresses intent through a search, such as “website development company Pune” or “SEO audit for clinic.” Search campaigns are strong when people already know what they need and are looking for a provider, product or answer.</p>
<h3>Meta Ads: discovery and audience attention</h3>
<p>People usually encounter Meta ads while browsing Facebook or Instagram feeds, Stories or Reels. Visual creative, audience strategy and repetition can introduce a problem or offer before the person searches for it.</p>

